@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Research
+
+## Scope and findings
+
+### Cart ownership and current-cart lookup
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java` exposes `POST /cart` and `PUT /cart/{code}` without reading the request principal. Both call the anonymous `ShoppingCartFacade` methods, so a token on those requests is ignored.
+- `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.addToCart(Customer, ...)` does set `customerId` for a newly-created customer cart, but the REST endpoint does not call it. `createCartModel` also supports customer ownership, so the existing facade can be reused.
+- `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.modifyCart(String, ...)` loads a cart by code and updates it without a customer context or ownership check. The customer-specific API therefore cannot safely use an arbitrary code.
+- `sm-core/.../ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getShoppingCart(Customer, MerchantStore)` queries all carts for the customer, filters out checked-out carts (`orderId != null`), and returns the first result. The repository query has no merchant-store predicate and no ordering, so it does not implement “most recently created or changed” deterministically.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl` is the v1 customer-cart adapter. Its optional `cart` parameter can merge an explicitly supplied cart, while the no-parameter path delegates to the service behavior above. This is the path used by `GET /auth/customer/cart`.
+- `ShoppingCart` has an audit section, but no explicit last-changed field used by the cart query. The database entity has `id`, which is monotonic for creation, but modifications do not change it. A `lastModified`/touch field or an equivalent update timestamp is needed to select the latest changed open cart.
+
+### Authenticated cart totals
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderTotalApi.java` gets the authenticated customer with `customerService.getByNick`, then gets the cart by store and ID and checks `customerId` ownership.
+- It correctly calls `orderService.caculateOrderTotal(orderSummary, customer, merchantStore, language)`, which is the customer-aware calculation used by checkout and therefore can apply the customer delivery address and tax.
+- The entire method is wrapped in `catch (Exception)` which calls `response.sendError(503, ...)`, including failures caused by `sendError(404, ...)` and service exceptions. This masks the intended 404 and causes the reported 503 behavior. The principal/customer lookup also uses a different customer lookup path from the cart API.
+
+### Authenticated checkout payment mismatch
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` loads the cart by code and calls `orderFacade.processOrder`.
+- `OrderFacadeImpl.processOrder` recalculates the order using the customer and cart, compares `Payment.amount` with the calculated total, and throws `ConversionException` with the calculated amount in the message before persisting/processing the order. This is the desired validation behavior.
+- The authenticated checkout controller catches every exception and converts it to `response.sendError(503, ...)`, unlike the guest flow’s validation response. It must preserve the payment mismatch as HTTP 400 and avoid proceeding with order creation. Ownership must also be checked before processing so one customer cannot check out another customer’s cart.
+- Successful processing eventually associates the cart with the order (`setOrderId`), so the open-current-cart query must exclude it after checkout.
+
+### Authenticated order list metadata
+
+- `GET /api/v1/auth/orders` calls `OrderFacadeImpl.getReadableOrderList(store, customer, page, count, language)` with `OrderCriteria.customerId` set.
+- `OrderRepositoryImpl.listByStore` filters by merchant and customer and orders by `o.id desc`; this supplies newest-first results and a count query. Pagination is based on `startIndex` and `maxCount`.
+- `OrderFacadeImpl.getReadableOrderList(OrderCriteria, ...)` returns immediately when the result list is empty after setting only `recordsTotal`; otherwise it copies `recordsTotal`, `totalPages`, and row metadata. The empty branch loses `totalPages`, and the shared `EntityList.getTotalPages()` returns 1 for zero pages, which conflicts with the required zero-page result. The customer endpoint’s `page` is currently passed directly as a start index, so it must be converted to the repository’s expected offset (`page * count`) or the criteria semantics must be made explicit.
+
+## Files expected to change
+
+- `sm-core-model/.../ShoppingCart.java` and `sm-core/.../ShoppingCartRepository.java` / `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java` for deterministic, store-scoped latest-open-cart selection and update timestamp support.
+- `sm-shop/.../ShoppingCartApi.java` and `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` for principal-aware cart creation/modification and ownership enforcement.
+- `sm-shop/.../OrderTotalApi.java` for customer ownership, customer-address total calculation, and correct 404/error propagation.
+- `sm-shop/.../OrderApi.java` for authenticated checkout ownership and HTTP 400 payment mismatch handling.
+- `sm-shop/.../OrderFacadeImpl.java` (and, if needed, the list model) for correct order-list pagination metadata.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- Anonymous cart requests must remain anonymous when no authenticated principal is present.
+- Explicit customer cart-code retrieval must remain constrained to the authenticated customer; it must not merge or expose another customer’s cart.
+- Checkout success must mark the cart checked out so it disappears from the customer’s current-cart lookup.
+- Existing guest total and checkout behavior should continue to use the same shared total calculation and validation messages.
+
